The classic problem! Here are a few solid ways:

**Flexbox (modern, most common):**
```css
.container {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center; /* horizontal */
  align-items: center;     /* vertical */
  height: 100vh;           /* or whatever height */
}
```

**Grid (clean, great for both axes):**
```css
.container {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center; /* centers both ways */
  height: 100vh;
}
```

**Absolute positioning (old school, still works):**
```css
.container {
  position: relative;
}

.div-to-center {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  left: 50%;
  transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
}
```

**Margin auto (horizontal only):**
```css
.div-to-center {
  margin: 0 auto;
  width: fit-content; /* or fixed width */
}
```

